  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 352 AM MDT Sun Sep 27 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\nA westerly flow aloft is trying to develop over Montana today. A\nweak upper level disturbance will also move through Southwest MT\nthis evening. This will result in a small chance for a\nshower/thunderstorm over Southwest MT tonight into Monday. Any\nprecipitation should be light.\n\nWith generally a westerly flow aloft this week, afternoon\ntemperatures will likely above normal Mon thru Fri across much of\nthe area. Additionally, expect winds to increase a bit as well for\nTue into Wed, creating elevated fire weather conditions over North\nCentral MT.\n\nFor next weekend, both the GFS/EC have a open upper level trof\nmoving through the CWA. The GFS has backed off on precipitation\nnext weekend as well. Thus there is only about a 20 percent chance\nfor a passing shower over the central and northern portions of \nthe CWA next weekend.\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\nThe main concern this week will be the increased winds once again\nfor Tue/Wed. Right now there is only about a 40 percent chance of\nwind gusts reaching high wind warning criteria on Tue evening.\nThus no high wind statement will be issued at this time.\n\nAdditionally, the increased wind gusts Tue, combined with low\nhumidity will allow for elevated fire weather conditions. Brusda",
